Does the graph shown represent direct variation, inverse variation, or neither? Justify your answer.

foundation.solution_text:
The graph is a curve that decreases as $x$ increases, and it gets closer to both axes without ever touching them.
This is the shape of inverse variation, $y=\dfrac{k}{x}$.
